*A refinement, (C+): every borrow by its final.* Finding 4 above stopped at a mechanism; there is a simple one, and it removes finding 2's residue. Detach every label held in $O$ alike: its sites below $O$ are dropped (with the frames below) and it gains a cell in frame 0 that reads its final; its sites in $O$ stay. For a label lent from below the cell replaces its sites below, as in (C); for an internal one it is an extra site, which in the checker is an identity fill, the sealed program $seal("loan"_ell)$ whose text is the hole (inside sealed programs a loan may occur any number of times, (X2)), and in the model a position reading $psi(ell)$, lent as a fill. Nothing accesses frame 0, so the extra site changes no run of the sides; at $ell$'s end it is filled and re-runs to $ell$'s final (D97). The footprint then compares the result, each _owned_ root at itself, and each _borrow_ root at its cell: no loan is ever followed outward, and `owners` is not used by `Id`. In a function's own check this changes `OwnRx` to `OwnR`'s form (`False`), so the two agree; elsewhere it changes only `Id`s over a borrow made in the observing frame whose loan sits under a fill, from the fill's equation to the final's.
- _Finding 2's residue goes._ The direct arm of a match in its frame $f$ compares, for a borrow root $r$, $r$'s final; the block in its own frame compares the final of its by-`&` capture of a place under $r$, a constructor path below $r$'s final (a capture is a place: a path of fields and `*` from a root). So the two `Id`s differ by `Eq`'s injectivity on constructors only, true in the model; no backward function's injectivity is used. A consumed internal borrow is the same label in both frames (the block takes it by move), compared at its cell in each.
- _DL needs no (I6)._ Every label of $O$ is treated alike, so the two detached states correspond through σ whatever the two sides' sites below were.
- _N1's relation R is no longer used by the argument._ Every use of a backward function's injectivity traced in this document is resolved determination (at call points, or within a frame at the block lemma) or the clause of membership that exists only because the model's function types demand it (@sec-tw-concl). Under (C+) neither remains, so the model can read a function type returning a borrow as all functions with a backward function, injective or not, and (X5) ("holes placed injectively") drops out of N5. D44 and D137 then express a choice about `'static` borrows, not a condition of soundness.
- _Verdicts_: the suite forms 19 `Id`s in a body over a borrow a call returned (`Equality.BadD18` and its twin among them, `ReturnedBorrows`' observations of a moved-out returned borrow); by reading, each keeps its verdict under (C+) (`BadD18`'s `e` becomes `False` in both arms instead of a conjunction over `Pick3`'s fills, still refuting its `refl` arm).
- _What it costs beyond (C)_: one more case in `detach`; the identity fill is a sealed program made on the observation's private copy by something other than [Close], so principle 7's "one maker" must say "held in the state outside an observation's copy" (it is filled and re-run before anything compares it). Not attacked beyond the rows of @sec-obs-attack, which it passes as (C) does.

*What I would choose: (C), refined to (C+).* It makes the observation a function of its own frame, so principle 6 holds for observations by construction instead of by tests at five sites, and principle 4's "one code, two runs" holds for `Id` by construction: the function's own check, a call site and a body run in place compute the same proposition from the same frame. Consistency loses its most delicate lemma at the place it was hardest (resolved determination over arbitrary caller states, with the fourth referee's three exclusions), the frame property loses its one exceptional clause, and C2's deferred-type gap closes; with (C+), resolved determination and the model's injectivity relation go altogether. The patch (B) keeps all of (A)'s obligations, adds two, and leaves one fault (`S4Z`) and a test whose only role is to keep a model that cannot read the fill from failing. The cost of (C) and (C+) is one kind of equation (finding 3), which a `rewrite` repairs and which no suite program uses.

*What I am unsure of.* (1) The completeness cost is measured on one shape by a proxy, and searched for in the suite's source (no program relies on it), not measured on the suite's verdicts; whoever builds (C) should dump every row's verdict against `main`. (2) (C+)'s identity fill in the checker: I argued it keeps (X2) and (WF12) on the copy by reading, not by running. (3) The model's `detach` and the lemma DL are not written in Lean; @sec-obs-dl sketches them against `SState`'s lending sites: under (C) DL needs one invariant the relation does not carry ((I6): a closure label is lent at a cell exactly when its image is lent in a caller's frame), under (C+) it does not; under both FR's (H8) must be stated of the labels σ may reorder rather than of the cells'.
